// Title: Suspicious Encoded PowerShell Command Line
// ID: ca2092a1-c273-4878-9b4b-0d60115bf5ea
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Markus Neis, Jonhnathan Ribeiro, Daniil Yugoslavskiy, Anton Kutepov, oscd.community
// Date: 2018-09-03
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
// Description: Detects suspicious powershell process starts with base64 encoded commands (e.g. Emotet)
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where ((((process.executable endswith "\\powershell.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\pwsh.exe")) or ((process.pe.original_file_name == "PowerShell.EXE" or process.pe.original_file_name == "pwsh.dll"))) and ((((process.command_line like "*_ JAB*" or process.command_line like "*_ SUVYI*" or process.command_line like "*_ SQBFAFgA*" or process.command_line like "*_ aQBlAHgA*" or process.command_line like "*_ aWV4I*" or process.command_line like "*_ IAA*" or process.command_line like "*_ IAB*" or process.command_line like "*_ UwB*" or process.command_line like "*_ cwB*")) and (process.command_line like "*_ -e*")) or ((process.command_line like "*_.exe -ENCOD *" or process.command_line like "*_ BA^J e-*"))) and not ((process.command_line like "*_ -ExecutionPolicy remotesigned *")))
